            <ArticleTitle>Contiguous multiple cervicothoracic spinous process fractures in an adult: A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>45-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jcot.2015.04.010</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fracture of isolated spinous processes at multiple levels is a rare injury. Herein, we present a 45-year-old male with cervical pain and swelling following a road traffic accident. Computerized tomography and magnetic resonance imaging revealed fractures of spinous process from C7 to D6 vertebra. The patient was managed with rest, analgesics and immobilization. At the 1-year follow-up, the patient is doing well without any neurological problem.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
